# Widgets & Composition

## Build method rules
- ✅ `build()` is pure UI description
- ✅ Extract:
  - complex UI blocks into private widgets
  - heavy calculations into helpers outside build (or memoize)
- ✅ Prefer `const` widgets/constructors
- ✅ Prefer `ConsumerWidget` for provider-driven UI; use `ConsumerStatefulWidget` only when you need local UI state/controllers
- ✅ If a widget does `await`, ensure you don’t use `context` after the await unless `mounted`/`context.mounted`

## State usage
- ✅ Use `StatefulWidget` only for ephemeral UI state:
  - animations, controllers, focus, local toggles
- ✅ App/business state lives in Riverpod notifiers/controllers

## Layout
- ✅ Use `LayoutBuilder` for responsive decisions
- ✅ Prefer `Sliver` patterns for complex scrolling
- ✅ Avoid deep nesting; create sub-widgets
- ✅ Prefer design tokens (e.g. `context.tokens.spacingM`) for spacing instead of magic numbers

## Keys
- ✅ Only use Keys when needed:
  - lists, reordering, animations, forms
- ❌ Don’t sprinkle keys everywhere

## NEVER
- ❌ Trigger navigation/dialog/snackbar directly in build
- ❌ Put data mapping logic in widgets
